            <abstract lang="en">
                <p>The coupling joins two pipe elements end to end using two complementary segments that enclose the pipe ends. Each segment has two lugs, one at each end, which align with the corresponding lugs on the other segment. Adjustable fasteners extend between the aligned lugs to draw the segments together. Each segment includes action surfaces facing the central pipe space and support surfaces on the lugs that interact with the fasteners. The action surfaces are perpendicular to the fastener axes, whilst the support surfaces are angled transversely. The angles of the support surfaces on opposite lugs slope are in opposite directions. Upon adjusting the first and second fasteners to draw the first and second segments toward one another, the opposite slopes of the first support surface and the second support surface cause the segments to rotate in opposite directions relatively to one another, and engagement between at least one of the first stop surfaces on the first lugs and the second stop surfaces on the second lugs arrests rotation of the segments relatively to one another.</p>
            </abstract>
